0,Indus Kohistani people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indus_Kohistani_people,"Indus Kohistanis are an Indo-Aryan ethnolinguistic group speaking the Indus Kohistani language. They mainly reside in Indus Kohistan, Hazara Division in northern Pakistan.","Kohistani, Indus",Indo-European
1,"Kohistani, Indus | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mvy/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..5rlhR-R4iUBVD8HeOoYV84fM97X4rl0v8RLOgb2LmGw,"Indus Kohistani is a stable indigenous language of Pakistan. It belongs to the Indo-European language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is taught as a subject of instruction in some schools.","Kohistani, Indus",Indo-European
2,Indus Kohistani - mvy (Indo-European) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/mvy/,"People Groups who primarily speak Indus Kohistani. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.","Kohistani, Indus",Indo-European
3,Indus Kohistani,https://grokipedia.com/page/Indus_Kohistani,"Indus Kohistani is a Dardic language belonging to the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European language family, spoken primarily along the western bank of the Indus River in the Kohistan region (now comprising the Lower Kohistan and Upper Kohistan districts)...","Kohistani, Indus",Indo-European
4,(PDF) Tone and song in Kalam Kohistani (Pakistan),https://www.academia.edu/1992277/Tone_and_song_in_Kalam_Kohistani_Pakistan_,"Kalam Kohistani exhibits five contrastive tones, challenging the perception of tonal languages in the region. The sung recitation of Kalam Kohistani poetry reveals a complex interaction between phonological tone and musical pitch.","Kohistani, Indus",Indo-European
5,The ASJP Database - Wordlist Indus Kohistani,https://asjp.clld.org/languages/INDUS_KOHISTANI,Wordlist Indus Kohistani. JSON. RDF serialized as n3.,"Kohistani, Indus",Indo-European
